cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "nutel: a neutrino-telescope toy for learning event reconstruction"
abstract: >-
  A two-dimensional neutrino telescope simulated from first principles ("Light in the Deep"): tracks, starting
  events, cascades and atmospheric muons emit Cherenkov light that is transported with switchable absorption and
  scattering to strings of optical modules and read out as hits and pulses; sampled detector families for
  multi-detector data sets, a documented HDF5 data format, analysis helpers and student tasks.
authors:
  - family-names: Gavrikov
    given-names: Arsenii
    affiliation: "Tsung-Dao Lee Institute, Shanghai Jiao Tong University"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArseniiGav/fm-nu-telescope"
url: "https://github.com/ArseniiGav/fm-nu-telescope"
keywords:
  - neutrino telescope
  - event reconstruction
  - Cherenkov light
  - photon transport
  - foundation models
  - particle physics
  - teaching
